From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sim: add regression tests for the scratch trailer scramble
 and the backwards-scramble boundary fixes (#1066)

Companion to 0004-scramble-scratch-trailer-and-backward-scramble-off-by-
one.patch, covering BOTH of its independent fixes:

  * scratch_trailer_cleared_after_swap runs a real, uninterrupted,
    permanent upgrade to completion on a flash device that does not
    require an explicit erase before rewrite (mcuboot host simulator,
    sim/, cargo + a C compiler, no embedded toolchain), and asserts the
    scratch area's temporary trailer never reads back with a GOOD magic
    afterwards. This exercises fix (i) -- the no-op erase replaced with
    swap_scramble_trailer_sectors() -- end to end, through the real swap
    machinery.

  * scramble_region_backwards_boundary calls boot_scramble_region()'s
    backwards branch directly instead, over an arbitrary sub-range of
    the scratch area, and asserts the write-block boundary at the low
    end of that range was actually written, and that nothing below it
    was touched. This is needed for fix (ii): every real bootutil
    caller reaches boot_scramble_region() only through
    swap_scramble_trailer_sectors(), whose off/size always sum to the
    flash area's own size -- the exact shape scratch_trailer_cleared_
    after_swap already exercises, and that end-to-end shape cannot
    distinguish "wrote the boundary block" from "silently dropped it"
    (verified: reverting just fix (ii)'s bootutil_area.c hunk left
    scratch_trailer_cleared_after_swap, and every other pre-existing
    sim test, still passing).

Getting there needed three new, additive pieces of sim plumbing, all
defaulting to today's behaviour for every existing test:

  * device_requires_erase(fa) (bootutil_area.h) is gated on
    MCUBOOT_SUPPORT_DEV_WITHOUT_ERASE / _WITH_ERASE. The simulator's own
    mcuboot_config.h never defined either, so every device the simulator
    ever built hardcoded device_requires_erase() == true regardless of
    erased_val -- the no-explicit-erase mechanism 0004 closes was
    unreachable by ANY sim test, not just an untested one. build.rs now
    defines both unconditionally, which switches the macro from a
    compile-time constant to the real runtime dispatch
    (flash_area_erase_required(), added to
    csupport/flash_map_backend/flash_map_backend.h), backed by a new
    SimFlash::erase_required (default true) plumbed through to C via
    sim_flash_erase_required() (mcuboot-sys/src/api.rs) the same way
    align/erased_val already are. A test opts a device out with the new
    SimFlash::set_erase_required(false), mirroring the existing
    set_verify_writes(false) escape hatch swap_size_erased_collision
    already uses for the same MRAM-is-directly-rewritable reason.

  * The STATE_0 branch 0004(i) fixes is itself gated on
    `!bs->use_scratch`, which requires the swapped image to NOT reach
    the trailer-holding sector(s) at the top of the slot -- slot >>
    image, matching AEN's real slot size (`DT_SIZE_K(2688)`,
    alp_e1m_aen801_m55_hp_ae822fa0e5597ls0_rtss_hp.dts) against a far
    smaller application. make_image() (the maker every other sim_test!
    in this file uses) cannot produce that: maximal() ignores its size
    argument and always returns ImageSize::Largest, so every existing
    image fills its slot to capacity and use_scratch is always true --
    verified empirically, zero
    `swap_scramble_trailer_sectors: fa_id=<scratch>` log lines across
    all 26 device/align/erased_val combinations with make_image(). Added
    ImagesBuilder::make_image_undersized(), a small, self-contained
    maker that calls install_image() directly with
    ImageSize::Given(4096) instead of maximal(), touching no other
    maker or test.

  * boot_scramble_region() itself is private to bootutil and has no
    Rust-callable surface. Added
    invoke_scramble_region_backwards_probe() (csupport/run.c): fills a
    flash area with a caller-chosen sentinel byte, calls
    boot_scramble_region(fa, off, size, backwards=true) directly over
    the area's last three write blocks, and reads back the byte at the
    range's own low boundary plus the byte one write block below it, so
    the Rust side can assert the boundary was written and nothing below
    the requested range was touched. Exposed as
    c::scramble_region_backwards_probe(), following the existing
    invoke_boot_go()/boot_go() extern-and-wrapper pattern.

Verified against the pinned upstream mcuboot revision
(6d3b3d2c38ab20c242e5b9abb04d050086383eb2, cargo 1.86.0 / gcc 13.3.0 on
WSL Ubuntu 24.04, ext/mbedtls submodule fetched at its pinned commit
2ca6c285a0dd3f33982dd57299012dacab1ff206), 0001-0003 applied first:

  * Pre-0004: `cargo test --release --test core` -- both new tests fail.
    scratch_trailer_cleared_after_swap fails on the very first
    device/align/erased_val combination it tries (the scratch area's
    temporary trailer reads back with a GOOD magic after a completed
    swap, exactly the self-perpetuating re-swap #1066 reported).
    scramble_region_backwards_boundary fails too (the boundary block it
    checks was never written).
  * With fix (i) applied but fix (ii)'s bootutil_area.c hunk alone
    reverted: 27 passed, 1 failed -- only scramble_region_backwards_
    boundary fails; scratch_trailer_cleared_after_swap and every other
    pre-existing test still pass, confirming fix (ii) needed its own
    direct test.
  * Post-0004 (both fixes applied): `cargo test --release --test core`
    -- 28 passed, 0 failed (26 pre-existing cases plus these two),
    across every device/alignment/erased_val {0x00, 0xff} combination
    each_device() sweeps.

Not wired into alp-sdk's own CI, for the same reason 0003 is not: needs
a Rust + C toolchain plus the ext/mbedtls submodule provisioned for the
vendored mcuboot checkout, a separate out-of-scope change. Reproduce
manually: `cd bootloader/mcuboot/sim && cargo test --release --test core
-- scratch_trailer_cleared_after_swap` and `... --test core --
scramble_region_backwards_boundary`. Upstream to mcu-tools/mcuboot then
drop alongside 0004.

Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
